evidence.quote:
Along every admissible sequence, with arbitrary normalized neutral ground states, for each fixed $a>0$, $$\label{tail:asymptotic-equation}
 s_\ell^3\int_{|y|>as_\ell}\rho_{\Psi_\ell}(y)\,\mathrm dy
       \longrightarrow \frac{b_{\mathrm{TF}}^3}{a^3}.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
Set $b_{\mathrm{TF}}=(81\pi^2/2)^{1/3}$. For every choice of normalized neutral ground states $(\Psi_Z)_{Z\ge1}$ of <a href="#intro:hamiltonian" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="intro:hamiltonian">[intro:hamiltonian]</a>, $$\begin{aligned}
 \lim_{m\to\infty}m^{1/3}
       \left[\limsup_{\substack{Z\to\infty\\ Z>m}}R_m(\Psi_Z)\right]
       &=b_{\mathrm{TF}},\label{intro:limsup}\\
 \lim_{m\to\infty}m^{1/3}
       \left[\liminf_{\substack{Z\to\infty\\ Z>m}}R_m(\Psi_Z)\right]
       &=b_{\mathrm{TF}}.\label{intro:liminf}
\end{aligned}$$ All limits are over integers. The inner limits hold $m$ fixed; no convergence in $Z$ at a fixed $m$ is assumed.

There are constants $D_0,Z_0<\infty$ such that every normalized neutral ground state with $Z\ge Z_0$ has offset at most $D_0$. For every fixed $0<\alpha<\beta<\infty$ and every $u>0$, its raw electron configuration satisfies $$\label{inp:counts}
 \begin{aligned}
 \left\|\#\{i:\alpha u<|x_i|<\beta u\}\right\|_{L^2(\mathbb P)}
 &\le C_{\alpha,\beta}
       \bigl(\max\{u^{-3},1\}+\sqrt{D_0u}\bigr),\\
 \mathbb E\#\{i:|x_i|>1\}&\le C(1+\sqrt{D_0}).
 \end{aligned}$$

There is a universal $C_{\mathrm{cap}}$ with the following property. Fix $L_1\ge2$, $0<h_l<h_h<\infty$, and $0<\xi<h_l/16$. For all sufficiently small $s>0$, depending on these parameters and $D_0$, and each $j<J$, there is an event in $\mathcal F_j$ whose complement has probability at most $Cr_j^{25}$, on which, simultaneously for $r_j\le |y|\le4L_1r_j$ and $h_l\le h\le h_h$, $$\label{inp:comparison}
 \begin{gathered}
 H_j(y)\le C_{\mathrm{cap}}|y|^{-4},\\
 |y|^6\mu_j(y)>kh^{3/2}
       \quad\Longrightarrow\quad |y|^4H_j(y)\ge h-\xi,\\
 |y|^6\mu_j(y)<kh^{3/2}
       \quad\Longrightarrow\quad |y|^4H_j(y)\le h+\xi.
 \end{gathered}$$ The probability constant may depend on the fixed comparison parameters, but $C_{\mathrm{cap}}$ does not. The estimates are uniform in $Z$, the ground state, $j$, and $J$.

The sequence $(F_\ell)$ is locally uniformly precompact on $\mathbb R^3\setminus\{0\}$. Every locally uniform subsequential limit $F$ is locally Lipschitz and satisfies $$\label{prof:limit-equation}
 \Delta F=f(F),\qquad F(x)\le C_{\rm cap}|x|^{-4},\qquad
 \frac1{4\pi}\int_{\mathbb S^2}F(d\omega)\,\,\mathrm d\omega\ge0
 \quad(d>0).$$ Along the same subsequence, $\sigma_\ell\to k(F_+)^{3/2}$ locally uniformly away from zero. Moreover, there is a constant $C_*$, depending only on $C_{\rm cap}$ and $k$, such that $$\label{prof:absolute}
 |F(x)|\le C_*|x|^{-4}\qquad(x\ne0).$$ The family of dilates $\{D^4F(D\,\cdot):D>0\}$ is also locally uniformly precompact away from zero.

Let $F$ be a continuous distributional solution of $\Delta F=4\pi kF^{3/2}$ on $\mathbb R^3\setminus\{0\}$, and suppose $$B|x|^{-4}\le F(x)\le C|x|^{-4}\qquad(x\ne0)$$ for constants $0<B\le C<\infty$. Then $$\label{prof:homogeneous}
 F(x)=A_*|x|^{-4},\qquad
 A_*=\left(\frac{12}{4\pi k}\right)^2=\frac{81\pi^2}{8}.$$ No radiality assumption is required.

For each fixed compact annulus $\mathcal A\subset\mathbb R^3\setminus\{0\}$, $$\sup_{\theta\in G_\ell}
 \left\|\sigma_\ell(\theta,\,\cdot)-\rho_*\right\|_{C(\mathcal A)}
 \longrightarrow0.$$ The corresponding assertion holds for $F_\ell(\theta,\,\cdot)-A_*|\cdot|^{-4}$.

For each fixed $0<a<b<\infty$, all sufficiently large $\ell$ satisfy $$\label{tail:localization}
 P_\ell(a,b)\le N_\ell(a/2,2b)$$ for every raw configuration. Moreover, for every fixed $0<\eta<\min\{a,(b-a)/2\}$, all sufficiently large $\ell$ satisfy $$\label{tail:sandwich}
 P_\ell(a+\eta,b-\eta)
    \le N_\ell(a,b)
    \le P_\ell(a-\eta,b+\eta)$$ for every raw configuration.

There is a constant $C$, independent of the fixed number $M>0$, such that every admissible sequence satisfies $$\label{tail:tightness-bound}
 \limsup_{\ell\to\infty}s_\ell^3
      \mathbb E\#\{i:|x_i|>Ms_\ell\}\le CM^{-3}.$$

Along every admissible sequence, with arbitrary normalized neutral ground states, for each fixed $a>0$, $$\label{tail:asymptotic-equation}
 s_\ell^3\int_{|y|>as_\ell}\rho_{\Psi_\ell}(y)\,\mathrm dy
       \longrightarrow \frac{b_{\mathrm{TF}}^3}{a^3}.$$
